{"id":"a1","level":2,"levelName":"Ulpan Alef","n":1,"of":19,"title":"Hello, and who you are","titleHe":"שָׁלוֹם","goal":"Greet someone and name yourself and them.","sections":[{"type":"text","body":"Hebrew separates you (m.) from you (f.) — there is no neutral second person. Which one you use depends on who you're speaking to, and you'll be choosing between them in every sentence from here on."},{"type":"table","caption":"Pronouns","head":["","singular","plural"],"rows":[["1st","אֲנִי — I","אֲנַחְנוּ — we"],["2nd m.","אַתָּה — you","אַתֶּם — you"],["2nd f.","אַתְּ — you","אַתֶּן — you"],["3rd m.","הוּא — he","הֵם — they"],["3rd f.","הִיא — she","הֵן — they"]]},{"type":"tip","body":"There is no word for am, is or are. אֲנִי מוֹרֶה is literally I teacher, and means I am a teacher."},{"type":"examples","items":[{"he":"שָׁלוֹם, אֲנִי דָּוִד.","en":"Hello, I'm David."},{"he":"מָה שְׁלוֹמְךָ?","en":"How are you? (to a man)"},{"he":"מָה שְׁלוֹמֵךְ?","en":"How are you? (to a woman)"},{"he":"הִיא מוֹרָה.","en":"She is a teacher."}]}],"vocab":[{"he":"שָׁלוֹם","en":"hello, peace","translit":"shalom"},{"he":"תּוֹדָה","en":"thank you","translit":"toda"},{"he":"בְּבַקָּשָׁה","en":"please, you're welcome","translit":"bevakasha"},{"he":"בֹּקֶר טוֹב","en":"good morning","translit":"boker tov"},{"he":"לְהִתְרָאוֹת","en":"see you, goodbye","translit":"lehitra'ot"},{"he":"כֵּן","en":"yes","translit":"ken"},{"he":"לֹא","en":"no, not","translit":"lo"},{"he":"מוֹרֶה","en":"teacher (m.)","translit":"more"},{"he":"מוֹרָה","en":"teacher (f.)","translit":"mora"},{"he":"סְטוּדֶנְט","en":"student (m.)","translit":"student"}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["hello, peace","west","work, craft","commandment, good deed"],"correct":0,"prompt":"שָׁלוֹם","translit":"shalom"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["duty, obligation","begins","thank you","of"],"correct":2,"prompt":"תּוֹדָה","translit":"toda"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["we will speak","narrative, legend","please, you're welcome","station, stop"],"correct":2,"prompt":"בְּבַקָּשָׁה","translit":"bevakasha"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["an emigrant","library","holiness","good morning"],"correct":3,"prompt":"בֹּקֶר טוֹב","translit":"boker tov"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["summer","family","therefore","see you, goodbye"],"correct":3,"prompt":"לְהִתְרָאוֹת","translit":"lehitra'ot"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["yes","Tishrei (Sept–Oct)","house","pays"],"correct":0,"prompt":"כֵּן","translit":"ken"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["reads","it is forbidden","no, not","his wife"],"correct":2,"prompt":"לֹא","translit":"lo"},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “student (m.)”?","options":["דִּירָה","חֹשֶׁךְ","סְטוּדֶנְט","בֵּינְתַיִם"],"correct":2,"he":true},{"type":"listen","q":"Which word did you hear?","options":["כֵּן","תּוֹדָה","מוֹרָה","סְטוּדֶנְט"],"correct":3,"say":"סְטוּדֶנְט","he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “please, you're welcome”?","options":["אִמָּא","בְּבַקָּשָׁה","מֶמְשָׁלָה","יָדוּעַ"],"correct":1,"he":true},{"type":"read","he":"שָׁלוֹם","translit":"shalom","en":"hello, peace"},{"type":"match","pairs":[["שָׁלוֹם","hello, peace"],["תּוֹדָה","thank you"],["בְּבַקָּשָׁה","please, you're welcome"],["בֹּקֶר טוֹב","good morning"],["לְהִתְרָאוֹת","see you, goodbye"]]},{"type":"listen","q":"Which word did you hear?","options":["לֹא","שָׁלוֹם","מוֹרָה","כֵּן"],"correct":0,"say":"לֹא","he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “no, not”?","options":["יוֹשֵׁב","הַרְגָּשָׁה","מַרְאָה","לֹא"],"correct":3,"he":true},{"type":"cloze","sentence":"___, אֲנִי דָּוִד.","en":"Hello, I'm David.","options":["מוֹרֶה","כֵּן","בְּבַקָּשָׁה","שָׁלוֹם"],"correct":3,"full":"שָׁלוֹם, אֲנִי דָּוִד."},{"type":"type","q":"Write “teacher (m.)” in Hebrew","answer":"מוֹרֶה","hint":"more"}]}